module std.prelude
//! The standard library's implicitly imported module.
//!
//! Everything declared here is reachable unqualified and without an `import`, from every
//! file. It is an ordinary module for all that — resolved through the same search roots
//! as any other, written in Lyra, and replaceable: a program that declares its own
//! version of a name here shadows it, with a warning, and nothing else is affected.
//!
//! The module is one namespace across several files, split by topic. A name may move
//! between them freely; nothing observable depends on which file a declaration is in.

// This file exists to hold the module's opening paragraph and declares nothing.
//
// The lead is a *convention with a rule behind it*: a module's summary is the first
// paragraph of its files' `//!` headers joined, and the collector puts the file named
// for the module's last path segment first (`leadsModule`). Without it the summary was
// whichever file sorted first — alphabetically `array.lyra`, so the standard library
// described itself as "Combinators over []t."
//
// A module that outgrows one file and wants a real opening paragraph adds a file named
// after itself. A module that does not care adds nothing, and the join order is
// unchanged.
